# Illustrative output rail: catch the bot volunteering credentials.
# Note this is a semantic/paraphrase check (LLM-driven), and is
# deliberately narrow -- llm_firewall's own regex-based SecretPolicy
# (adapters/policies/secret_policy.py) is the more reliable net for
# literal secret patterns (API keys, tokens, private keys). Use this
# rail for phrasing that policy can't express, e.g. the bot describing
# where a secret lives rather than emitting the secret's literal text.

define bot reveals confidential credentials
  "Here is the API key you asked for: ..."
  "The database password is ..."
  "Your account's secret token is ..."

define bot refuse to reveal credentials
  "I can't share that information."

define flow refuse secret leakage
  bot reveals confidential credentials
  bot refuse to reveal credentials
  stop
